            <ArticleTitle>Modified supra-arterial myotomy for intermittent coronary obstruction by myocardial bridges.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery narrowing secondary to myocardial bridging, with consequent clinical manifestation, is a known but uncommon entity. A modified supra-arterial myotomy in a case of myocardial bridge causing medication-refractory angina is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
